{
    "pageid": 3314,
    "title": "Hospital",
    "sections": [
        {
            "heading": "Introduction",
            "level": 1,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Hospitals are special holdings , exclusive to The Reaper's Due DLC, which are used to increase disease resistance in a province, as well as decrease the chance of depopulation. They will also safeguard prosperity in a province by decreasing the chance of outbreaks of diseases to occur or spread to the province."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Hospitals can provide their owner with several other resources as well, such as piety, tech points, opinion modifiers, etc. Having a hospital in a province will also allow several hospital-related events to occur, such as allowing a Court Physician to improve their skills."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Building a hospital",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Non-nomadic or tribal rulers can build a hospital in their controlled territory for a base cost of 100 wealth. Note: If a hospital is built in a vassal's territory, or if it finished building after you have given the county away, the hospital is still considered yours and will be stuck in your buildings list."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Alternatively, you can spend 300 piety and allow a holy order to build a castle in your capital in exchange for a hospital there. This is accessed by right-clicking a holy order captain and selecting \"Invite to Build Hospital\"."
                }
            ]
        },
